ient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, making up to 3 attempts in total. I checked it against a local HTTP server and it behaves as intended.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `urllib` raises a 503 as an `HTTPError`. The client catches it and closes the error response before retrying.\n- The wait between attempts doubles each time: 0.5s after the first failure, then 1s.\n- On the third attempt the 503 is raised to the caller, so failures stay visible instead of being hidden.\n- Any other status (500, 404 and so on) is raised straight away with no retry.\n- Network errors and timeouts are not retried; I kept to exactly what was asked.\n- Two new constructor settings control this: `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. They have defaults, so existing calls don't change.\n\n**Results from the local test server (backoff set to 0.05s):**\n\n| Scenario | Result | Server hits |\n|---|---|---|\n| Success on first try | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned after ~0.15s | 3 |\n| 503 three times | 503 raised | 3 |\n| 500 | raised immediately | 1 |\n\nI didn't add a test file because the project doesn't have a test setup.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70457, "requests_cache_write": 142426, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7634574, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1859, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial12", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 82, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:45.759210+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.365, "t_checker_s": 2.389, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none